  "features": [
    "Both HTTPS and tls.Server decode ALPN callback names as ASCII and select the original offered wire bytes by length-prefix offset, preserving first-match behavior for aliases. Negotiated protocol getters decode opaque bytes as Latin-1.",
    "HTTPS constructor accepts deferred callback types like Node while preserving truthy callback/list conflict rejection; later validation and accepted-socket receiver remain incomplete.",
    "Corpus dispatch forwards all supported test-name filter aliases through single/multiple-file, directory and subset routes. Ordinary integration controls verify excluded bodies do not execute, and missing/invalid/no-match patterns fail.",
    "The complete valid ALPN control passes on Node and Home. Final native groups include both expanded callback and corpus-filter discovery controls."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "HTTPS accepted-TLSSocket receiver and callback lifecycle/error/reload behavior remain open in #875/#532.",
    "The first TLS name-selection attempt ran 38 cases because filters were dropped; it receives no filtered-scope credit. After forwarding, only one case passes and 37 are filtered, but JUnit encodes them as skips while process counters show zero skips. Strict validation remains failed; filtered-case accounting and remaining corpus CLI options are tracked in #876.",
    "No original corpus assertion was modified. Eight selected original files match pinned source bytes. The seven-file baseline retains #874: 60 passes plus three process checks and one registered failure/failed file. It is not green.",
    "Disk admission refusal and terminal cache cleanup are retained. Initial ordinary filter controls failed as expected on the prior binary; directory-fixture inventory and route-summary expectations were corrected without relaxing body-execution assertions.",
    "Pickier has no errors and five existing style warnings. Zig fmt reports the same existing server callback formatting on the committed baseline; other modified Zig files pass. Logs are retained.",
    "Previously excluded constructor/Deno regression files were not rerun and remain unverified. Full suite, #872 and Release/ASAN/all-platform coverage remain open under #66."
  ],
